class.description:
[DialogueLocalization] is a resource that loads and manages multilingual dialogue data from JSON files.

Each dialogue is identified by a unique ID and can include text, typing speed, pauses, expressions, etc. for multiple languages (locales).

[b]JSON structure example:[/b]
[codeblock]
{
    "SANS_CALL_1": {
        "ko": {
            "text": ["* 전화 받았습니다", "* WA sans"],
            "speed": [0.05],
            "pauses": [
                { "index": 6, "duration": 1.0 }
            ]
        },
        "en": {
            "text": ["* Call answered", "* WA sans"],
            "speed": [0.03]
        },
        "expressions": [0, 1]
    }
}
[/codeblock]

[b]Usage example:[/b]
[codeblock]
var dialogue_data = DialogueLocalization.new()
dialogue_data.load("res://dialogues/battle.json")

# Get dialogue in current system language
var dialogue = dialogue_data.get_dialogues_default("SANS_CALL")

# Get dialogue in specific language
var dialogue_ko = dialogue_data.get_dialogues("ko", "SANS_CALL")
[/codeblock]

[en] For a more detailed explanation, please refer to the tutorials linked below.
[ko] 이것보다 더 자세한 설명(또는 한국어 문서)은 아래 링크된 튜토리얼을 참고하세요.
